===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To make or become less [[serious]] and more [[cheerful]] or [[casual]]; to [[relax]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=6 Aug 83 |journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Michael Bronski|title=Gay Sensibility, Straight Imitation|text=Sondheim's sense of life — which is pretty pessimistic (I don't think that anyone ever ends happily ever after in a Sondheim musical) — is brought through without trying to '''lighten it up'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=w:Adele|title=First Love
|passage=you '''lighten up''' my heart when I start to cry}}
#: ''I wish he'd '''lighten up''' a bit and realize that we were only joking.''

